      "side": 1,
      "message": "That is the way they are implemented in the C++ backend as far as I know; and that is how I implement the endianness in the python backend.\nWe discussed with David about adding a construct to make it clearer to the user what is being packed together when endianness is applied, e.g.\n\n```\npacket Test {\n    packed {\n    a: 2,\n    b: 14,\n    }\n}\n```\nThis change is just to ensure that the current semantic is well-defined until we decide if we want to make the change.",
